.07, "lead_after": 30.08, "points_lost": 0.01, "best": "J4"}, {"turn": 63, "color": "B", "move": "E7", "lead_before": 30.08, "lead_after": 30.13, "points_lost": -0.05, "best": "A8"}, {"turn": 64, "color": "W", "move": "pass", "lead_before": 30.13, "lead_after": 30.08, "points_lost": -0.05, "best": "pass"}, {"turn": 65, "color": "B", "move": "pass", "lead_before": 30.08, "lead_after": 30.0, "points_lost": 0.08, "best": "A9"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "A Left-Edge Crawl While the Centre Stayed Open", "summary": "Black, the 20k, won by 30 points after two passes. The game was close early, but between turns 18 and 30 GPT-6.1 Sol kept answering on the left edge. The engine's first choice was G4 or H6 for most of those moves, and the lead swung between +4.8 and +41.0 as both sides lost 10 to 35 points a move. GPT-6.1 Sol averaged 8.6 points lost per move against the 20k's 7.3, and the final position had no captures.", "moments": [{"turn": 10, "text": "The game was level at -0.7 after the 20k's D2, then White's B4 lost 14.4 points and pushed the lead to +13.7. The engine wanted B5. Black took B5 next, and the 20k's lead only grew from there."}, {"turn": 24, "text": "B8 lost 24.5 points, taking the lead from +16.4 to +41.0. White was extending along the left edge at B7 and B8 while the engine preferred G4, out in the open on the right."}, {"turn": 27, "text": "The 20k's B6 was the worst move of the game, losing 34.6 points and dropping the lead from +39.4 to +4.8. The engine's choice was H6. For one move White was almost back in the game."}, {"turn": 28, "text": "White did not take the chance. A7 lost 23.2 points and sent the lead back up to +27.9. The engine's choice was H4, away from the edge fight."}, {"turn": 56, "text": "J8 lost 22.1 points, moving the lead from +7.9 to +30.0, and the engine's choice was A1. Black's later A1 then lost nothing, and the lead held near +30 through the two passes."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script was a helper: the `inspect`/`playSave` functions parsed returned boards into groups, liberties and empty regions and logged them, then a replay of the actual played moves, an area count and file writes (log, SGF, review, AGENTS.md) followed. None of it looped over candidate moves, played out continuations, or ranked or recommended a move, so all move choices stayed manual.", "stop": false}}